<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ dollar, bill rates climb on RBNZ statement.</title>
<headline>NZ dollar, bill rates climb on RBNZ statement.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand dollar climbed sharply, 90-day bank bill rates rose and futures were sold after the Reserve Bank's economic forecasts at 9 a.m. on Friday (2100 GMT Thursday).</p>
<p>Reserve Bank Governor Don Brash said a monetary policy easing was &quot;off the agenda&quot;.</p>
<p>			  BEFORE (2055 GMT)	 AFTER (2150 GMT)</p>
<p>NZ dollar		US$0.6929/36		 US$0.6956/63</p>
<p>Trade-Weighted Index     65.82			  66.04</p>
<p>90-day bills		  9.77			   9.86</p>
<p>11/06 bonds		   8.29			   8.31</p>
<p>Dec futures		  90.83			  90.73</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
